            <ArticleTitle>Extrapleural catheters: an effective alternative for treating postoperative pain for thoracic surgical patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>15-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1053/j.semtcvs.2012.04.009</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain control is an important aspect of video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery (VATS) procedures. Offering an effective and low-risk method of postoperative pain control is thus vital to a patient's recovery. Hotta and colleagues report the results of a clinical study comparing efficacy of epidurals vs extrapleural catheters in VATS procedures. They found that extrapleural catheters provided equivalent postoperative pain relief when compared to thoracic epidural catheters.</AbstractText>
